// M5-A3P-1010. Ch20 U07 "The Cage" (P boss, 12 min), the arrival. act3_ch20.md §2 U07, §5; glossary.
// The four founders who bound themselves (Orin Tesk, Halde Moor, Isse Varan, Cael Imbrey), each chained into a seat of
// bound light round a well: the cage is the boss's body. Nothing about them is monstrous except what they're bound into
// (rule 4). TOMA HOLDS THE LINE (a locked-active set piece like Ch8's stair and Ch16's line; his Swell primed if
// ch14_toma_refused). The founders speak only Lamptongue phrases, which Ysolde translates in the help line, except "thank
// you", said in the common tongue (ch20_bark_vowbound_fights). "Cage-Wardens" is retired (act3_threads T-05).
title: ch20_the_cage
location: ch20/undertow_layers
---
@letterbox on
@camera U28
@music the_cage fade=2.0
@vfx glimmer_bound at=cage_seats count=4
@wait 5.0
Ysolde [neutral]: Four seats. Four of the six. They bound themselves here first. #line:ch20_cage_001
@wait 2.0
@mark toma cage_line walk
Toma [determined]: I'll hold the line. Break the seats. #line:ch20_cage_002
@letterbox off
<<event start_battle ch20_the_cage>>
===
